From a8501e9dc9003b0153cff5f021af0c534aa083fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?R=C3=A9gis=20LELOUP?= <neonunux@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 22:22:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add hinge angle sensor support, reporting tablet mode

Read the hinge angle of convertibles from IIO hinge sensors, like the ones
of hid-sensor-custom-intel-hinge, and report laptop or tablet mode through
a uinput SW_TABLET_MODE switch, as suggested in #318: libinput handles it
like a kernel provided switch, and desktops switch to their tablet mode.

- drv-iio-poll-hinge polls the in_angl0 channel labelled "hinge" every
  100 ms, after letting the sensor settle for 1.5 s when started;
- tablet mode is reported from 200 degrees and laptop mode up to 170, after
  two readings; a closed lid and a tablet folded flat, which look the same
  to the sensors, are told apart by where the hinge came from, the lid
  switch only deciding on startup;
- the switch is not created if the kernel already reports tablet mode;
- the hinge is tracked whether or not clients claimed sensors, and keeps
  the accelerometer running: the ITE sensor hub of Lenovo Yoga convertibles
  only updates the hinge angle while it is enabled.

Tested on a Lenovo Yoga 910-13IKB.

Closes: #318

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
